{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["ויישם — like ויושם. And similarly: וייקץ, like ויוקץ. From (ישב) (MS variant: שוב) — ויושב. From יצא — המוצאים. היא מוצאת. From ירד — והורד המשכן." "In a coffin — he was buried in the ground, for they were destined to bring him up in a coffin. When His wrath and fury turned away from them, and they crossed the Jordan — with joy and song, rose of the Sharon. And thus ויחי is completed. I pour out my thoughts, for my praise and glory, to strengthen my strength — restore my outcast! Though I lost my eternal — from the belly of Him who brings forth, moon of my fragrance, from the pit — send only! Words in their entirety. The book is completed — from the mouth of their abundant master, until he himself elevated it — tablets exalted, a humble man fashioned. And at the head of these Names: the foundation of wisdoms — mockeries to fools! He who clothes the Rock, head of nations, with bands — for Him the remnant of heat — shall rebuild the souls, forged like figs, from the cunning, dust of the walls, and whole stones, all fitted together — atonement for guilts, embittered souls, shall rebuild within walls, on the mountain from places — and they shall not offer the fats of beasts upon the high places."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {0 "The note '(ישב) (נ\"א שוב)' records a manuscript variant: one witness reads שוב instead of ישב as the root. Rashbam is listing examples of אהוי-weak roots whose hifil forms appear in Biblical Hebrew with vav-conversive.", 1 "Comment 1 is textually problematic: after the brief peshat remark on 'in a coffin,' the Hebrew transitions into rhymed liturgical/poetic verses (punctuation: רון/שרון, שיחי/שבחי/כחי/נדחי/נצחי/גוחי/ניחוחי/שלחי, etc.), which appear to be a scribe's colophon or later addition rather than Rashbam's commentary. The text is possibly corrupt; I translate hyper-literally, preserving the rhymed sections as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:05.710214352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}